  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total obligations are $1.7B for FY2026 to date. Award count is 28,271 and average award size is $60K. Obligations fell 31.8% year over year. FY2026 to date obligations are lower than prior full fiscal years: FY25 obligations were $2.5B, FY24 obligations were $3B, FY23 obligations were $2.7B, FY22 obligations were $2.4B, and FY21 obligations were $2.6B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in Minnesota with obligations of $540M. The Department of Agriculture obligated $279M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $276M. NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION is the largest vendor by obligations at $192M. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $192M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $140M and Cheese Manufacturing at $93M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did FY2026 to date compare with prior years?",
        "body": "FY2026 to date obligations are $1.7B, down 31.8% year over year. FY25 obligations were $2.5B and FY24 obligations were $3B, showing that FY2026 to date is below the last two full fiscal years. FY23 obligations were $2.7B, FY22 obligations were $2.4B, and FY21 obligations were $2.6B, so FY2026 to date sits below each of those totals. All figures are contract obligations and the FY2026 total is partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who buys and who gets the most federal contract money in Minnesota?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $540M, the Department of Agriculture obligated $279M, and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $276M. NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION received $192M, MCGOUGH CONSTRUCTION CO., LLC received $106M, and CUMMINS POWER GENERATION INC. received $85.4M. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing accounted for $192M, Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounted for $140M, and Cheese Manufacturing accounted for $93M. These figures reflect FY2026 to date contract obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
